@assert fib_memo(90) == 2880067194370816120
@assert fib_memo(100) == big"354224848179261915075"
@assert try fib_memo(-1); false catch e; e isa ArgumentError end
```

The memo table lives in the enclosing call, so there is no global state and each call starts fresh. `get!` with a `do` block computes a missing value once and stores it. The recursion depth is `n`, so for very large `n` an iterative loop is the better choice.

