@assert divisor_sum(36) == 91
```

Divisors come in pairs `(d, n/d)`, so scanning only up to `isqrt(n)` finds all of them in O(sqrt n); the `q != d` test avoids double-counting a square root. A perfect number's divisor sum, including itself, is exactly 2n.

