@assert balanced("f(x[i]) { return 1; }")
@assert !balanced("(]")
@assert !balanced("(()")
```

A stack of open brackets is the natural structure: every closer must match the most recent unmatched opener, and the stack must be empty at the end. Non-bracket characters are ignored. The check is O(n); `pop!(stack)` is guarded by the `isempty` test so a stray closer returns `false` rather than throwing.

